@startuml

title One bundle publish: dependency order, one function per dataset

hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left

actor "Operator" as op
participant "ores.shell" as sh
queue "NATS" as n
participant "ores.dq\npublish handler" as dq
participant "publish\nservice" as ps
database "DQ\nregistries" as reg
participant "workflow\nengine" as wf
participant "target service\npublish handler" as th
database "PostgreSQL" as db

== The request ==

op -> sh : bundles publish world --wait
sh -> n : dq.v1.ops.publish_bundle\n{bundle, tenant, params}
n -> dq : publish_bundle
dq -> dq : authorise dq::datasets:write
dq -> ps : list the bundle's publishable datasets
ps -> reg : members, artefact types,\ndependency edges
reg --> ps : members in display order, edges
ps -> ps : resolve the dependency closure;\ndrop a dataset with no target subject
ps --> dq : datasets, in dependency order
dq -> dq : drop an optional member\nthe run did not opt into
dq -> wf : start bundle_publish_workflow,\none step per dataset
dq --> sh : instance id

== The run, one step per dataset ==

loop each dataset, in dependency order
    wf -> th : the dataset's subject
    th -> db : ores_<c>_publish_<p>_from_dq_fn\n(dataset, target tenant, mode, params)
    db -> db : read the artefact rows\nfrom the system tenant
    opt the dataset is party-scoped
        db -> db : resolve the party: params,\nthen the tenant's root party,\nthen the system party
    end
    db -> db : upsert the row in the target tenant,\nstating the dataset in the commentary
    db --> th : inserted, updated, skipped, deleted
    th --> wf : the step's counts
    note right of wf
        A step commits its own function call.
        A failed step stops the run, and the
        steps already committed stay.
    end note
end

wf --> dq : the run is terminal
sh -> n : workflow.v1.ops.get_workflow_steps\n(or the --wait reply)
n --> sh : step states and counts
sh --> op : what each dataset wrote

== The same function, at bring-up ==

note over db
  The bootstrap calls the same functions,
  as the database owner, after the schema
  and the artefact rows are loaded.
  No bus, no workflow, no tenant.
end note

@enduml
